{"name":"Witch Hazel","hex":"#fbf073","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"witch hazel","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several small deciduous trees, of the genus Hamamelis, having yellow flowers\n Hamamelis virginiana, native to eastern North America.","Hamamelis virginiana, native to eastern North America."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/witch_hazel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Witch Hazel (Looney Tunes)","blocks":[{"text":"Witch Hazel is an animated cartoon character in the Warner Bros. Looney Tunes and Merrie Melodies series of cartoons and TV shows. Witch Hazel is a fairy tale witch antagonist with green skin, a round figure, exaggerated bulbous facial features, and a single tooth. The name is a pun on the witch-hazel plant and folk remedies based on it."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/f3/Witch_Hazel_%28Looney_Tunes%29.jpg/330px-Witch_Hazel_%28Looney_Tunes%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Witch_Hazel_(Looney_Tunes)"},{"title":"Witch-hazel","blocks":[{"text":"Witch-hazels or witch hazels (Hamamelis) are a genus of flowering plants in the family Hamamelidaceae, with three species in North America, and one each in Japan (H. japonica) and China (H. mollis). The North American species are occasionally called winterbloom."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Hamamelis_virginiana_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-070.jpg/330px-Hamamelis_virginiana_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-070.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Witch-hazel"},{"title":"Witchcraft","blocks":[{"text":"Witchcraft is the use of magic by a person called a witch. Traditionally, \"witchcraft\" means the use of magic to inflict supernatural harm or misfortune on others, and this remains the most common and widespread meaning. Though the idea of witchcraft is largely imaginary, it has nevertheless served in many cultures as a way to explain the presence of evil. The belief in witches has been found throughout history in a great number of societies worldwide. Most of these societies have used protective magic or counter-magic against witchcraft, and have shunned, banished, imprisoned, physically punished or killed alleged witches. Anthropologists use the term \"witchcraft\" for similar beliefs about harmful occult practices in different cultures, and these societies often use the term when speaking in English."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/John_William_Waterhouse_-_Magic_Circle.JPG/330px-John_William_Waterhouse_-_Magic_Circle.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Witchcraft"},{"title":"Hazel","blocks":[{"text":"Hazels are plants of the genus Corylus of deciduous trees and large shrubs native to the temperate Northern Hemisphere. The genus is usually placed in the birch family, Betulaceae, though some botanists split the hazels into a separate family Corylaceae. The fruit of the hazel is the hazelnut; the trees are also grown as ornaments in hedges or gardens."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Corylus_avellana_0001.JPG/330px-Corylus_avellana_0001.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hazel"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/60/Witch_Hazel_transformed.png/330px-Witch_Hazel_transformed.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/60/Witch_Hazel_transformed.png/330px-Witch_Hazel_transformed.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Transformed into a female rabbit, Witch Hazel gets Bugs Bunny's attention in 